 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives those of a named substrate."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"e2260c14-9d75-4bba-b98a-6c649aaa3dad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The style is a list of ",
 Cell[BoxData["Graph"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1eeadcb4-c46b-42a5-84be-d558e963f67f"],
 " option rules: ",
 Cell[BoxData["VertexStyle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "a71e6327-eb82-4c13-979a-435336bd3109"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["EdgeStyle"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b77f228c-eee7-47ef-9b73-bc145fb88e9d"],
 " in the causal-graph colours of the Wolfram Physics Project (events ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Hue", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0.11", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0.97"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f2d0ca8e-5be7-436d-aebc-d6f3aca20805"],
 ", causal edges ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Hue", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0.56"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f484abe5-a49f-4b68-be58-985168cf4b71"],
 ", the values of SetReplace's ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<CausalGraph\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5b0bc6a7-d70a-4ecf-b4db-9e059a9fa9ca"],
 " style and of the causal graphs of the Technical Introduction) with \
arrowheads, a ",
 Cell[BoxData["VertexSize"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "93c25551-f2ad-4969-ae8d-05a8ab49755c"],
 " that shrinks with the size so that larger graphs stay legible, and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"GraphLayout", " ", "->", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"\"\<LayeredDigraphEmbedding\>\"", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Orientation\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "Bottom"}]}], "}"}]}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0abff4a3-7f49-49ac-9793-057ccde5a99a"],
 ", which draws a directed acyclic graph in layers with time upward. It is \
the analogue of InfraGeometry's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateStyle"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateStyle", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "81c0b66a-c906-47b2-89c1-76373ba8ce70"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0168712d-3410-491d-80b7-976100927b98"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The style depends on the size alone: every named substrate of one size has \
the same colours, and the edge opacity and the arrowheads shrink with the \
size. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CausalSubstrate"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/CausalSubstrate", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "3f269b03-553a-4950-addd-d793d078a33c"],
 " applies it, and so does ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["RandomCausalGraph"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/RandomCausalGraph", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8adbca86-525b-4f95-b1ea-c008fb8062b1"],
 ", with the size chosen by the number of events (",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Small\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f94d548e-74b6-4137-83c3-f6482ddf40a2"],
 " up to 250, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Medium\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3a95d7e1-d8ea-4e7f-b129-d1ef677e0fa0"],
 " up to 800, ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Large\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e0dbcc4-3bdf-47d7-b477-d6cb9b1573d7"],
 " beyond). A layout given by ",
 Cell[BoxData["VertexCoordinates"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4bddbed9-4722-4b1c-bb7e-d53af1549f26"],
 ", as under ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\"\<KeepCoordinates\>\"", " ", "->", " ", "True"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f0dbde38-88e4-49eb-ba15-388816529ebf"],
 ", takes precedence over the layered embedding."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a2a76715-26e0-4574-afba-aa95ac99e295"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Highlights read best in the same palette: light cones, light rays and the \
current slice of a foliation in ",
 Cell[BoxData["Red"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "aae7c7be-d3a8-4532-84e3-917c49c826e2"],
 ", the colour of the causal cones and foliations of the Technical \
Introduction; the past in the Project's blue ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"RGBColor", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0.259", ",", " ", "0.576", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6326a985-6bfd-4c3c-95cb-5873eaa33fc6"],
 "; worldlines and observers in ",
 Cell[BoxData["StandardBlue"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01c4c328-bb1c-441c-8570-9e8cc3e4f7d4"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData["StandardGreen"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1b4dd370-316c-4a88-80ef-183d697cb872"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"6d175f58-0feb-4b8a-9427-f4ddb81fd41c"]
}, Open  ]],

